---
import ToolPageLayout from '../layouts/ToolPageLayout.astro';
import SeparationPayCalculator from '../islands/SeparationPayCalculator';
import laborJson from '../data/labor/2026.json';
import type { LaborRules } from '../lib/rules/types';
import { computeSeparationPay } from '../lib/engine/terminalPay';
import { peso } from '../lib/format';

const labor = laborJson as unknown as LaborRules;
const meta = labor.meta;
const SP = labor.separation_pay;
const HANDBOOK = SP.source_url;
const pays = [15000, 20000, 25000, 30000, 40000];
const yearsList = [1, 3, 5, 10];
const exR = computeSeparationPay({ monthlyPay: 25000, years: 7, cause: 'one-month' }, labor);
const exH = computeSeparationPay({ monthlyPay: 25000, years: 7, cause: 'half-month' }, labor);

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How is separation pay computed in the Philippines?', a: `Multiply your latest monthly pay (basic salary plus regular allowances) by the rate for your cause of termination and by your credited years of service — a fraction of at least ${SP.fraction_months_counted_as_year} months counts as a whole year. The rate is one month per year for ${SP.one_month_causes.slice(0, 2).join(' and ').toLowerCase()}, and half a month per year for ${SP.half_month_causes.slice(0, 3).map((c) => c.split(' ')[0]!.toLowerCase()).join(', ')} and the other Art. 299 causes. It can never be less than ${SP.min_months} month's pay (DOLE Handbook, Ch. 14).` },
  { q: 'How much separation pay for redundancy after 7 years at ₱25,000?', a: `Redundancy pays one month per year: ${peso(25000)} × 1 × 7 = ${peso(exR.separationPay)}. Had the cause been retrenchment (half a month per year) it would be ${peso(exH.separationPay)}. Seven years and seven months would count as eight years.` },
  { q: 'Which causes get one month per year and which get half a month?', a: `One month per year of service: ${SP.one_month_causes.join('; ')}. Half a month per year: ${SP.half_month_causes.join('; ')}. (Labor Code Arts. 298–299, as summarised in the DOLE Handbook.)` },
  { q: 'Is separation pay due when I resign or am dismissed for cause?', a: 'No. Separation pay is owed only for termination on authorized causes under Arts. 298–299 (and by analogy where a court orders it). Resignation and dismissal for just cause carry no separation pay unless a company policy, CBA or contract grants it; you are still owed your final pay — unpaid salary, pro-rated 13th month and leave conversions.' },
  { q: 'Is separation pay taxable?', a: 'No. Under Sec. 32(B)(6)(b) of the Tax Code, amounts received because of separation for death, sickness, disability or any cause beyond the employee\'s control — including redundancy, retrenchment and closure — are excluded from gross income and exempt from income tax (DOLE Handbook, Ch. 14-F).' },
  { q: 'When must the employer pay, and what notice is required?', a: `The employer must serve written notice on both the employee and the DOLE regional office at least one month before the termination date (RKS Form 5 or the DOLE Establishment Report System). Separation pay is part of the final pay, which DOLE Labor Advisory 06-20 says should be released within ${labor.final_pay.release_days} days of separation.` },
  { q: 'Magkano ang separation pay kung 5 taon at ₱20,000 ang sahod?', a: `Depende sa dahilan: redundancy o labor-saving devices = ${peso(computeSeparationPay({ monthlyPay: 20000, years: 5, cause: 'one-month' }, labor).separationPay)} (isang buwan kada taon); retrenchment, closure o sakit = ${peso(computeSeparationPay({ monthlyPay: 20000, years: 5, cause: 'half-month' }, labor).separationPay)} (kalahating buwan kada taon). Hindi ito bababa sa isang buwang sahod, at exempt sa income tax.` },
];
---

<ToolPageLayout
  title="Separation Pay Calculator Philippines 2026 – Art. 298 & 299"
  description="Compute separation pay: one month per year of service for redundancy and labor-saving devices, half a month for retrenchment, closure or disease, never below one month — per the DOLE Handbook."
  path="/separation-pay-calculator/"
  h1="Separation Pay Calculator Philippines"
  faqs={faqs}
  related={['finalPay', 'sssUnemployment', 'thirteenth', 'retirementPay']}
>
  <Fragment slot="answer">
    <p>
      <strong>Separation pay</strong> is your latest monthly pay × a rate set by the cause × credited years of service:
      <strong>one month per year</strong> for redundancy, installation of labor-saving devices and impossible reinstatement;
      <strong>half a month per year</strong> for retrenchment, closure not due to serious losses, disease and lack of
      assignment (Labor Code Arts. 298–299). A fraction of at least {SP.fraction_months_counted_as_year} months counts as a
      year, and the result is never below {SP.min_months} month's pay. Example: ₱25,000, 7 years → {peso(exR.separationPay)} for
      redundancy, {peso(exH.separationPay)} for retrenchment. It is exempt from income tax.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="calculator">
    <SeparationPayCalculator client:idle />
  </Fragment>

  <h2>Separation Pay Table (One Month per Year)</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Monthly pay</th>{yearsList.map((y) => <th>{y} yr{y === 1 ? '' : 's'}</th>)}</tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {pays.map((p) => (<tr><td><strong>{peso(p)}</strong></td>{yearsList.map((y) => <td>{peso(computeSeparationPay({ monthlyPay: p, years: y, cause: 'one-month' }, labor).separationPay)}</td>)}</tr>))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Halve these amounts for the half-month causes, but never below one month's pay.</p>

  <h2>Authorized Causes and Their Rates</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>One month per year of service:</strong> {SP.one_month_causes.join('; ')}.</li>
    <li><strong>Half a month per year of service:</strong> {SP.half_month_causes.join('; ')}.</li>
    <li><strong>Salary base:</strong> the latest salary rate including regular allowances — not basic pay alone (Handbook Ch. 14-D, citing Planters Products v. NLRC).</li>
    <li><strong>Minimum:</strong> one month's pay whatever the length of service.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Notice, Release and Tax</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Written notice to the employee <strong>and</strong> the DOLE regional office at least one month before the termination date.</li>
    <li>Paid with the <a href="/final-pay-calculator/">final pay</a>, which DOLE expects within {labor.final_pay.release_days} days of separation, together with unpaid salary, pro-rated 13th month pay and unused leave conversions.</li>
    <li>Exempt from income tax under NIRC Sec. 32(B)(6)(b) when the separation is for a cause beyond the employee's control.</li>
    <li>Involuntarily separated SSS members may also claim the <a href="/sss-unemployment-benefit-calculator/">SSS unemployment benefit</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Official Source</h2>
  <p>
    Labor Code of the Philippines, Arts. 298–299, as summarised in the
    <a href={HANDBOOK} target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOLE Handbook on Workers' Statutory Monetary Benefits, 2024 edition, Chapter 14</a>
    (NWPC mirror). Rules data: <a href={meta.official_source_url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{meta.official_source_label}</a>.
    AyTool is independent; for a dispute, file with the DOLE regional office (Single Entry Approach) or the NLRC.
  </p>
</ToolPageLayout>
